id: git-checkout
name: Git checkout
description: <folder>.git-checkout.json at the cell root marks <folder>/ as a Git checkout kept without .git
  (remote, branch, commit). Read this handler's skill (handler_skills) before any git operation on the folder
  (diff, log, blame, compare with the remote, sync or push).
types:
- ext: .git-checkout.json
guidance: A <folder>.git-checkout.json at the cell root records the Git checkout in <folder>/ with exactly about,
  remote (the repository's clone address, https://host/path, ssh://user@host/path or user@host:path, never with a
  user name, password or token on https), branch and commit (the full SHA of the remote commit the folder's files
  are based on). The Git Clone / Update and Git Push runners write it; nothing else edits it. The cell never holds
  .git. Skills teach agents to run git in a temporary blobless clone of the remote outside the cell at the recorded
  commit, reading the cell folder only as a work tree through a temporary index, and never running a command that
  writes the work tree; to rely on the Git account's credential the app places in the environment (a token's
  header in GIT_CONFIG_COUNT, or for an SSH key on this machine GIT_SSH_COMMAND naming the key file and trusting
  only the account's own server) and never to print it, read the key file, change the ssh options, rewrite an
  address to SSH themselves or put a credential in a URL, on argv or in a file; never to create .git in the cell or
  commit or push from the temporary clone; and to ask the user to run Git Clone / Update to bring in the remote's
  changes and Git Push to publish. A file of this type inside a folder is that repository's own content and is not
  checked.
examples:
- folder: cloned
  description: The record Git Clone / Update writes beside the folder api/ it describes.
  expect: valid
  feedback: Exactly about, remote, branch and commit, with commit a full commit SHA.
- folder: nested-group
  description: A record for a GitLab project in a nested group.
  expect: valid
  feedback: A GitLab project path keeps every group.
- folder: ssh-remote
  description: A record for a Git server reached over SSH on port 2222.
  expect: valid
  feedback: A Git server reached over SSH records its ssh:// address with its user and port.
- folder: scp-remote
  description: A record for a Git server named by its scp address, relative to the SSH user's home.
  expect: valid
  feedback: An scp address (user@host:path) is recorded as typed; git sends its path unchanged.
- folder: added-field
  description: A record carrying a field the runners never write (a url).
  expect: invalid
  feedback: A record holds exactly about, remote, branch and commit; nothing else, and never a token.
- folder: branch-for-commit
  description: A record whose commit is a branch name instead of a commit SHA.
  expect: invalid
  feedback: commit is the full 40- or 64-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA of a commit.
- folder: credentials-in-remote
  description: A record whose https remote carries a user name and token.
  expect: invalid
  feedback: remote never carries a user name, password or token; credentials live in Key manager.
- folder: bare-path
  description: A record whose remote is owner/name without a server.
  expect: invalid
  feedback: remote is the clone address the runners record (https://host/path, ssh://user@host/path or user@host:path).
- folder: repository-content
  description: A file of this type inside a cloned folder, which is that repository's own content.
  expect: valid
  feedback: Only a file at the cell root is a checkout record; a nested one is not checked.
